* stsj.scheme
* dash translation of Stata's stsj scheme.
*
* PROVENANCE
*   Source Stata scheme : /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/s/scheme-stsj.scheme
*                         (#include chain, outermost first: s2color -> s2mono -> stsj)
*   Style files         : /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/style
*   Stata version       : StataNow 19.5 (MP), born 12 Aug 2026
*   Extracted           : 2026-09-19 (fixture generated_utc 2026-09-19T16:13:55Z)
*   Derived from        : test/fixtures/scheme_truth.json ["stsj"],
*                         generated by scripts/extract_scheme_truth.py
*   Last true as of     : the Stata version and date above.  Re-run the
*                         extractor and re-check this file against the fixture
*                         after any Stata upgrade.
*
* WHY HEX AND NOT STATA COLOUR NAMES
*   Every colour below is written as a RESOLVED #rrggbb value, already looked up
*   through Stata's own color-*.style files.  dash's OptionTranslator._COLOR_MAP
*   knows only 72 Stata colour names, and SchemeParser._color() silently returns
*   its "#000000" default for any token it cannot resolve.  Hex is self-contained
*   and cannot be swallowed that way.
*
* Property categories used by dash SchemeParser:
*   color, symbol, linepattern, linewidth, intensity, gsize, graphsize,
*   symbolsize, clockdir, numstyle

label "Stata Journal (stsj)"

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Background and region colors
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
color background      #ffffff
color plotregion      #ffffff
color legend          #ffffff
color legend_line     #ffffff
color major_grid      #e8e8e8
color minor_grid      #505050
color heading         #000000
color axisline        #000000

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Per-plot color cycle (p1-p15), from "color p1".."color p15"
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
color p1      #606060
color p2      #a0a0a0
color p3      #808080
color p4      #404040
color p5      #000000
color p6      #c0c0c0
color p7      #202020
color p8      #707070
color p9      #909090
color p10     #b0b0b0
color p11     #d0d0d0
color p12     #505050
color p13     #303030
color p14     #c0c0c0
color p15     #505050

* Per-plot line color (for line/connected plots).
* stsj sets no per-plot "color p#line"; all 15 resolve through the stub
* directive "color pline", which is black.  Spelled out per index because
* SchemeParser reads "color p#line" by exact key and implements no fallback.
color p1line   #000000
color p2line   #000000
color p3line   #000000
color p4line   #000000
color p5line   #000000
color p6line   #000000
color p7line   #000000
color p8line   #000000
color p9line   #000000
color p10line  #000000
color p11line  #000000
color p12line  #000000
color p13line  #000000
color p14line  #000000
color p15line  #000000

* Per-plot `twoway line` colour  [Stata: color p#lineplot]
* /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/s/scheme-s2mono.scheme:103 declares one stub
* directive, `color plineplot black`, covering all 15 plots.  It is the
* line colour of `twoway line`, reached through style/linestyle-p#line.style
* (`set color scheme p#lineplot`).  dash's SchemeParser
* implements no p#stub -> pstub fallback, so it is spelled out per plot,
* exactly as the `color p#line` block above is.
color p1lineplot   #000000
color p2lineplot   #000000
color p3lineplot   #000000
color p4lineplot   #000000
color p5lineplot   #000000
color p6lineplot   #000000
color p7lineplot   #000000
color p8lineplot   #000000
color p9lineplot   #000000
color p10lineplot  #000000
color p11lineplot  #000000
color p12lineplot  #000000
color p13lineplot  #000000
color p14lineplot  #000000
color p15lineplot  #000000

* Per-plot bar/area fill color.  stsj sets no "color p#bar"; each resolves
* through the fallback chain to "color p#" (identical to the p cycle above).
color p1bar    #606060
color p2bar    #a0a0a0
color p3bar    #808080
color p4bar    #404040
color p5bar    #000000
color p6bar    #c0c0c0
color p7bar    #202020
color p8bar    #707070
color p9bar    #909090
color p10bar   #b0b0b0
color p11bar   #d0d0d0
color p12bar   #505050
color p13bar   #303030
color p14bar   #c0c0c0
color p15bar   #505050

* Per-plot marker fill color (scatter).  Same story as the bar cycle: no
* "color p#mark" in stsj, so each resolves to "color p#".
color p1mark   #606060
color p2mark   #a0a0a0
color p3mark   #808080
color p4mark   #404040
color p5mark   #000000
color p6mark   #c0c0c0
color p7mark   #202020
color p8mark   #707070
color p9mark   #909090
color p10mark  #b0b0b0
color p11mark  #d0d0d0
color p12mark  #505050
color p13mark  #303030
color p14mark  #c0c0c0
color p15mark  #505050

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Marker symbol cycle, from "symbol p1".."symbol p15"
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
symbol p1     circle
symbol p2     diamond
symbol p3     square
symbol p4     triangle
symbol p5     x
symbol p6     plus
symbol p7     circle_hollow
symbol p8     diamond_hollow
symbol p9     square_hollow
symbol p10    triangle_hollow
symbol p11    smcircle
symbol p12    smdiamond
symbol p13    smsquare
symbol p14    smtriangle
symbol p15    smx

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Line patterns.  stsj sets no per-plot "linepattern p#line"; all 15 resolve
* through the bare "linepattern p" default, which is solid.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linepattern p1line   solid
linepattern p2line   solid
linepattern p3line   solid
linepattern p4line   solid
linepattern p5line   solid
linepattern p6line   solid
linepattern p7line   solid
linepattern p8line   solid
linepattern p9line   solid
linepattern p10line  solid
linepattern p11line  solid
linepattern p12line  solid
linepattern p13line  solid
linepattern p14line  solid
linepattern p15line  solid

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Line patterns for `twoway line` plots  [Stata: linepattern p#lineplot]
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Stata does not read a plain `twoway line` plot's line from the
* `p#line` scheme keys.  It reaches the `p#lineplot` keys through two
* style files:
*   style/seriesstyle-p#line.style:5   set line    scheme p#line
*   style/linestyle-p#line.style:4-7   set width   scheme p#lineplot
*                                      set color   scheme p#lineplot
*                                      set pattern scheme p#lineplot
* So `linepattern p#lineplot` is the dash pattern of `twoway line`, while
* the `linepattern p#line` block above is what style/linestyle-p#.style
* reads -- the connecting line of `twoway connected`.  Stata documents the
* three keys in scheme_line_plots.sthlp:29-34 as the colour, thickness and
* pattern "for #th line plot".
*
* Stata also documents `linewidth p#lineplot`; no base scheme declares
* it, so there is none to translate and dash keeps reading `linewidth p`.
*
* Source: /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/s/scheme-s2mono.scheme:132-146,
*         reached through the #include chain s2color -> s2mono -> stsj.
* These 15 patterns are why three overlaid `twoway line` plots under this
* scheme are drawn solid / dash / vshortdash rather than three solid lines.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linepattern p1lineplot   solid
linepattern p2lineplot   dash
linepattern p3lineplot   vshortdash
linepattern p4lineplot   longdash_dot
linepattern p5lineplot   longdash
linepattern p6lineplot   dash_dot
linepattern p7lineplot   dot
linepattern p8lineplot   shortdash_dot
linepattern p9lineplot   tight_dot
linepattern p10lineplot  dash_dot_dot
linepattern p11lineplot  longdash_shortdash
linepattern p12lineplot  dash_3dot
linepattern p13lineplot  longdash_dot_dot
linepattern p14lineplot  shortdash_dot_dot
linepattern p15lineplot  longdash_3dot

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Line widths (Stata style names; the fixture's numeric .30 is in undocumented
* Stata linewidth units and is deliberately not transcribed here)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linewidth p           medium
linewidth major_grid  medium

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Fill intensities
* "intensity area" is not set by stsj (nor by any Stata base scheme); it
* resolves through the bare "intensity" class default, which is full.  Written
* under the explicit "area" key because SchemeParser reads that exact key.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
intensity p        inten80
intensity bar      full
intensity area     full

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Font sizes (Stata gsize keywords; relative-unit values not transcribed)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gsize text          medium
gsize heading       large
gsize axis_title    medsmall
gsize tick_label    medsmall
gsize note          small

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Graph dimensions, in inches (consumed by section 10 for figure proportions)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
graphsize x  3.575
graphsize y  2.6

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Default marker size for the p cycle
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
symbolsize p  medium

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Legend placement
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
clockdir legend_position  6
numstyle legend_cols      2

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Grid visibility (Stata `yesno` directives)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
yesno draw_major_hgrid      no
yesno draw_major_grid       no
